 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2021-03-02",
   "text": "Background Check Expansion Act\n This bill establishes new background check requirements for firearm transfers between private parties (i.e., unlicensed individuals).\n Specifically, it prohibits a firearm transfer between private parties unless a licensed gun dealer, manufacturer, or importer first takes possession of the firearm to conduct a background check.\n The prohibition does not apply to certain firearm transfers, such as a gift between spouses in good faith."
  }
 ],
